---
layout: layouts/page.njk
permalink: /about/
title: "About the Firm"
heading: "Bridging environmental responsibility and practical implementation."
description: "Geosustara Enviro Services LLP — environmental and geospatial consultants in Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala, serving industry, government and academia."
lede: "We were founded to close the gap between environmental responsibility and practical implementation, by delivering integrated environmental and geospatial solutions rather than reports alone."
showCta: true
sections:
  - { id: overview,     label: Overview }
  - { id: vision,       label: Vision & Mission }
  - { id: who-we-serve, label: Who we serve }
  - { id: approach,     label: Approach }
  - { id: questions,    label: Questions }
breadcrumbs:
  - text: Home
    url: /
  - text: About
faqs:
  - q: "What does Geosustara Enviro Services LLP do?"
    a: "We are a sustainability-driven environmental consulting firm. Our work covers environmental compliance and auditing, Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and Environmental Clearance (EC) support, GIS, remote sensing and thematic mapping, water, wastewater and solid waste management, sustainability consulting, and technical support for research and academic projects."
  - q: "Who do you work with?"
    a: "Industries and manufacturing units, quarries and mineral-based industries, hotels and commercial establishments, government agencies and local bodies, residential communities, research organizations, and students and academic institutions."
  - q: "Where are you based and where do you work?"
    a: "Our office is at Perekonam, Pappanamcode, Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala. We work with clients across India, with most site work in Kerala and neighbouring states."
  - q: "How does an engagement usually run?"
    a: "In four stages — assessment, planning, implementation and monitoring. We support clients from the initial site investigation through to continuous monitoring rather than handing over a report and leaving."
  - q: "Do you carry out both the study and the engineering?"
    a: "Yes, and that is deliberate. Environmental site investigation, GIS and remote sensing, and treatment system design sit in one team, so the data behind an assessment is the same data a design is sized on."
---
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import svcIcon, arrow, picture -%}

<section class="sec" id="overview">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="svc-layout">
      <div class="svc-body prose rv">
        <p class="svc-intro" style="margin-bottom:34px">Geosustara Enviro Services LLP is a sustainability-driven
          environmental consulting firm committed to helping organizations achieve regulatory compliance, optimize
          resource use, and adopt responsible environmental practices.</p>

        <h2>The gap we exist to close</h2>
        <p>{{ site.whyUs.problem }}</p>
        <p>{{ site.whyUs.answer }}</p>

        <h2>Beyond reports</h2>
        <p>We provide end-to-end services that go beyond reports. Our approach combines technical expertise, field
          experience, scientific analysis, and a deep understanding of evolving environmental regulations to deliver
          practical, cost-effective, and sustainable solutions.</p>
        <p>Because environmental engineering, site investigation and geospatial analysis sit inside the same team,
          an assessment we write and a treatment system we size are built on the same field data — rather than on
          two sets of numbers that have to be reconciled at the end.</p>

        <h2>What our expertise covers</h2>
        <p>Our expertise spans environmental engineering; Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and Environmental
          Clearance (EC) support; environmental site investigation; GIS, remote sensing and mapping; water quality
          assessment and reporting; wastewater treatment and reactor design; solid waste management; CADD and
          technical design; sustainability consulting; and technical support for research and academic projects.</p>
        <ul class="xp" style="margin:22px 0">
          {%- for e in site.expertise %}
          <li><a href="{{ ('/services/' + e.s + '/') | url }}"><span class="d" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ e.t }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>

        <h2>What we believe</h2>
        <p>At Geosustara, we believe sustainability should be practical, measurable, and impactful. We support our
          clients from initial assessment and planning through implementation and continuous monitoring, transforming
          environmental challenges into opportunities for responsible growth and innovation.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="svc-side">
        {% include "partials/secnav.njk" %}

        <div class="side-card">
          <h3>Our services</h3>
          <ul>
            {%- for s in services %}
            <li><a href="{{ ('/services/' + s.slug + '/') | url }}">{{ s.shortTitle }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="side-card">
          <h3>Registered office</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><span>{{ site.contact.addressLine }}</span></li>
            <li><span>{{ site.contact.locality }}, {{ site.contact.region }} {{ site.contact.postalCode }}</span></li>
            {%- for p in site.contact.phones %}
            <li><a href="tel:{{ p.e164 }}">{{ p.display }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
            <li><a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== VISION / MISSION ===================== -->
<section class="sec sec--tint" id="vision">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="label">Our purpose</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">What we are working toward.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="vm">
      <div class="vmc rv">
        <span class="vmi">{{ svcIcon("globe") }}</span>
        <h3>Vision</h3>
        <p>{{ site.vision }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vmc rv">
        <span class="vmi">{{ svcIcon("target") }}</span>
        <h3>Mission</h3>
        <p>{{ site.mission }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pullquote rv">Expertise you can trust. Engineering <em>backed by evidence</em>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== WHO WE SERVE ===================== -->
<section class="sec" id="who-we-serve">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="label">Who we serve</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Who we work with, and<br>what each one usually needs.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">The problems differ by sector far more than the regulations do. These are the starting
        points we are asked about most often.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="serve rv">
      {%- for s in site.whoWeServe %}
      <li>
        <h3>{{ s.t }}</h3>
        <p>{{ s.d }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== APPROACH ===================== -->
<section class="sec sec--tint" id="approach">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="label">How we work</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">From first survey to<br>continuous monitoring.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">Our approach combines technical expertise, field experience, scientific analysis and a deep
        understanding of evolving environmental regulations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lc-grid">
      <div class="lc-sticky">
        <div class="lc-vis">
          {{ picture("panel", "Satellite view of a shallow coastal strait used as a survey reference panel.",
                     [640,1000], "(max-width:1040px) 460px, 40vw", "lazy", false, 1000, 1000) }}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" aria-hidden="true">
            <g id="lcg"></g>
            <path id="lctrail" fill="none" stroke="#16C264" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="4 5" opacity=".5" d=""></path>
            <circle id="lcring" cx="200" cy="200" r="34" fill="none" stroke="#16C264" stroke-width="1.4" opacity=".7"></circle>
            <circle id="lcdot" cx="200" cy="200" r="5" fill="#16C264"></circle>
          </svg>
          <span class="lc-stage" id="lcStage">Stage 01 — Assessment</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lc-steps">
        {%- for st in site.lifecycle %}
        <div class="lc-step{{ ' on' if loop.first }}" data-stage="Stage {{ st.n }} — {{ st.title }}">
          <span class="n">STAGE {{ st.n }}</span>
          <h3>{{ st.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ st.body }}</p>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== FAQ ===================== -->
<section class="sec" id="questions">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:900px">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="label">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Common questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq rv">
      {%- for f in faqs %}
      <details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ f.q }}</summary>
        <div class="a">{{ f.a }}</div>
      </details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
